  "question": {
    "text": "Let $\\left(1+x+x^2\\right)^{10}=a_0+a_1 x+a_2 x^2+\\ldots .+a_{20} x^{20}$. If $\\left(a_1+a_3+a_5+\\ldots .+a_{19}\\right)-11 \\mathrm{a}_2=121 \\mathrm{k}$, then k is equal to $\\qquad$ ."
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "239",
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\left(1+x+x^2\\right)^{10}=a_0+a_1 x+a_2 x^2+\\ldots .+a_{20} x^{20}$\n$\\therefore 3^{10}=\\mathrm{a}_0+\\mathrm{a}_1+\\mathrm{a}_2+\\ldots .+\\mathrm{a}_{20}$   ...(i)\n$1=a_0-a_1+a_2 \\ldots . .+a_{20}$   ...(ii)\n$\\text { (i) - (ii) } \\Rightarrow a_1+a_3+\\ldots .+a_{19}=\\frac{3^{10}-1}{2}=29524$\n$\\begin{aligned}\n\\text { Also }\\{ & 1+\\mathrm{x}(1+\\mathrm{x})\\}^{10}=1 \\\\\n& +{ }^{10} \\mathrm{C}_1 \\mathrm{x}(1+\\mathrm{x})+{ }^{10} \\mathrm{C}_2 \\mathrm{x}^2(1+\\mathrm{x})^2+\\ldots .\n\\end{aligned}$\n$\\therefore \\mathrm{a}_2={ }^{10} \\mathrm{C}_1+{ }^{10} \\mathrm{C}_2=55$\n$\\therefore \\frac{\\left(\\mathrm{a}_1+\\mathrm{a}_3+\\ldots+\\mathrm{a}_{19}\\right)-11 \\mathrm{a}_2}{121}=239$"
  }
